# CSA Loom — Trivy CRITICAL-gate baseline (SC1)
#
# The blocking build gate (build-fiab-images-acr-tasks.yml "Trivy gate") reads
# this file. Every entry is a KNOWN, REVIEWED finding that the gate ignores,
# with the reason and the burn-down path. Adding an entry requires the same
# review a guard-allowlist entry gets: an ignore is a LOAN, not a fix — it must
# name the upstream that would clear it and be removed the moment that ships.
#
# ── BASELINE IS EMPTY (B-SC1', loom-apex, 2026-07-28) ──────────────────────
# All three baselined CVEs were burned down by fixing the images, not by
# widening this file. Kept below as the audit trail.
#
#   CVE-2026-59873 — node-tar gzip-bomb DoS, in the copy of node-tar VENDORED
#     inside npm in the node base images (loom-console, loom-copilot-maf,
#     loom-mcp-bridge). Fixed in tar >= 7.5.19, first bundled by npm 11.18.0 —
#     and NO node base image ships a patched npm yet (node 22.23.1 -> npm
#     10.9.8 -> tar 7.5.11; node 26.5.0 -> npm 11.17.0 -> tar 7.5.16, both read
#     out of the published npm tarballs on registry.npmjs.org). A base bump
#     alone would NOT have cleared it, so it was resolved per image:
#       - loom-console / loom-copilot-maf / loom-onelake / lineage-extractor:
#         the runtime never invokes a package manager, so npm + npx are DELETED
#         from the final layer — the vulnerable code is gone, not muted.
#       - loom-mcp-bridge: it SPAWNS npx at runtime, so npm is upgraded in
#         place to the patched 11.18.0 (ARG NPM_VERSION in its Dockerfile).
#
#   CVE-2024-47561 — Apache Avro deserialization, in avro-1.11.3.jar vendored
#     by the upstream Debezium Connect base (loom-mirroring). Base bumped
#     quay.io/debezium/connect 3.0.0.Final -> 3.5.2.Final, which carries
#     avro-1.12.0.jar via apicurio-registry 2.6.13.Final (both converter
#     tarballs listed off Maven Central before the bump).
#
#   CVE-2026-33845 — libgnutls30 DTLS reassembly OOB read in the loom-mcp-bridge
#     OS layer. Debian fixed it in gnutls28 3.7.9-2+deb12u7 (bookworm) /
#     3.8.9-3+deb13u4 (trixie) per the Debian security tracker. The bridge
#     Dockerfile's leading `apt-get update && apt-get dist-upgrade -y` (landed
#     in #2527) pulls deb12u7 ahead of the pinned base tag, so the CVE is moot
#     in the built image — the entry was stale, not deferred.
#
# Node majors: node 20 "Iron" hit EOL 2026-04-30 and Docker Hub froze every
# node:20* tag on 2026-04-22, so every Loom node image moved to node 22 "Jod"
# (LTS through 2027-04-30). Next base-image review is due before that date.
#
# Do NOT add an entry here to make a build go green. Fix the image, or open the
# gate's emergency valve (skip_supply_chain) with an incident note.
